Somewhere in the depths of the Dungeons of Doom,
there's a quiet liquor shop where the potions of
booze are ever-renewing, and the shopkeeper keeps
setting them up as long as the adventurer keeps
forking over the zorkmids. In this shop can be found
up to half a dozen other peaceful characters, also
enriching the, let's call her a "bartender" and be
done with it. It implements the new #tip command,
when you really, really needs someone to listen to
your sorrows.

Here the #chat is all about the YASDs past and the
YASDs yet to come. About the cursed bags of tricks
and unIDed but riskily read scrolls of genocide,
about the PC-provoked summoning storms and being
cornered by a flock of MMFs without a can of grease
to your name. About bags of holding that went
"poof", amulets of reflection left in a sack, and
"oLS that went unworn.

This isn't the demi-gods' bar.

This is the bar for the rest of us: the demi-dunce's
bar. The place where scrolls of amnesia are read
willingly, treated like liferings tossed to a
water-walker who forgot to wear his water walking
boots.

The bar where PCs go to forget.

It could sit in a little reserved corner of Mine's
End, or up a set of stairs marked "members only"
from one of the "tiger" doors in toplevel Sokoban.

It could be the place you go when the RNG wins
again without bothering to break a sweat.

